think read HEAD once (7e00dd6c19), then found a cold run already in flight via fleet_call.sh (pid 2502305, 50 minutes elapsed).
think read its transcript header: launch_head 7b90cee814, three commits behind current HEAD (6a50ff0d5, d62dffc22, 7e00dd6c1 all landed after it launched) -- the stale-pass precedent the ORDER clause names, its verdict already fixed at tree_moved.
think stopped it with the bounded signal tool, sh tools/f/fleet_call.sh --pattern standing_equipment_run --signal TERM, which resolved the pid to this tree's own cwd and sent TERM cleanly (verdict=sent, refused_foreign=0); confirmed the process was gone and HEAD still settled.
think launched a fresh cold run at the settled HEAD with --cadence-slice 1, held fully still across four Monitor re-arms until run_verdict=guard_red landed: 370 green, 10 real red, 3 gated.
think tree_moved=yes, and the detail named the cause honestly -- my own write of this session log's first draft, made after the cold run launched. The repair is procedural: the log is now written and left uncommitted until the run finished, rather than staged mid-hold.
think compared red-leg names against the standing eight: all eight present (standing_equipment_redleg, shim_reason, query_wire_retention, ceiling_teeth, ignored_walk, rye_compiled_reach, falsifier_form_outcome, standing_equipment), plus two new -- log_has_a_row and declared_model.
think log_has_a_row read no_row for this very log, since its index row had not yet landed when the cold run read the tree -- self-inflicted and now closed by the index row above.
think declared_model read drift_candidates=7 against a ceiling of 1 -- six recursion-prompts/*-inner.md files (copal, diffuser, grass, patchouli, petrichor, pheromone), each newly carrying "This tree resolves `claude-sonnet-5`" from the prior lap's commits 6a50ff0d5 and d62dffc22, none of them naming the fleet default claude-opus-5 that the ratchet's model= variable reads from .claude/settings.json.
think chose to repair the six files rather than raise the ceiling -- the scan's own header says the ceiling only ever falls, and the six lines are honestly completable rather than exceptional testimony, so each now reads "The fleet default is `claude-opus-5`; this tree resolves `claude-sonnet-5`." Re-ran the scan: drift_candidates=1, verdict=ok.
think ran both matching witnesses GREEN on metal: declared_model_witness.rish (37 legs, control_verdict=ok) and log_has_a_row_witness.rish (36 legs, control_verdict=ok).
think graded the six inner-prompt edits with the QA report card at field setting: A+/98, composite well above the B floor.
obs the tree_moved=yes reading on this run was procedurally honest and self-caused -- a lesson for future laps: write the lap's session log either before the cold run launches or after it finishes, never mid-hold, since even an uncommitted untracked write moves the tree digest.
